//! **Owner: lane DEC** (deconstruct and studies, wave 4). Pre-declared by lane S0l (R2).
//!
//! "Deconstruct this preset" lessons, generated by ablation (docs/learn.md, "Deconstruct lessons (lane DEC)"; report
//! 01 §6; report 03 §9): take each element out of the preset, measure what the sound loses, drop what is inaudible,
//! then rebuild the rest in signal-flow order, each step heard without and with its element and rebuilt by ear.
//!
//! | Piece | Where | Pure? |
//! | --- | --- | --- |
//! | Elements, the base, projection | [`element`] | yes: parameter space only |
//! | The planner, [`plan()`](plan::plan)`(preset, ranks)` | [`plan`] | yes: the caller measures the ranks |
//! | The measurements (ablations, steps in context, sound items, "What disappeared?") | [`measure`] | renders through `enth-render`, no I/O, clock or thread |
//! | The lesson, its patches and automatic text | [`build`] | as [`measure`] |
//! | The authoring TOML (`lesson.toml`) | [`toml_out`] | yes |
//! | The runtime entry point for a user's preset, [`auto_lesson`] | here | as [`measure`] |
//!
//! `lesson-gen deconstruct` (`tools/lesson/src/gen.rs`) calls [`build::generate`] at authoring time and writes the
//! factory studies (`content/lessons/studies/`), whose text is then edited by hand. **The plugin's worker calls
//! [`auto_lesson`]** on a user's preset: one call measures, plans and builds a one-lesson pack in memory, verified by
//! the same reader as any pack, so the session plays it as it plays a bundled lesson (`Pack::bundle`, then the
//! player). It costs a few hundred renders (the report counts them), so it is a background job with progress, never
//! live.

pub mod build;
pub mod element;
